{"gates": {"G1": true, "G2": true, "G3": true, "G4": true, "G5": true, "G7": true}, "green_means": {"G1": "the source compiles and every part exports with the default parameters, with no errors, failed asserts, timeouts or warnings", "G2": "every part is a closed mesh: watertight, 0 bad edges, no inverted shells, a positive volume and the declared number of bodies", "G3": "the assembly: each instance is its part moved (same volume, area and principal moments), every part placed as many times as its copies, no overlap between instances beyond the allowed_interferences, all of them one connected group, the units the request chains, and every instance the spec says is held (all the printed parts, printed in place) held by the others: none comes off moving straight along any of 26 directions, though one freed by turning first is not caught (nothing to check for one part without an assembly)", "G4": "every declared motion swept through its whole range (a screw advancing as it turns, the instances it drives at their ratio) and stopped, past each end it declares a stop, by a collision within 2 mm of travel; at each rest it declares, its flex free, and between two rests riding over what it presses on; and every assembly_order step brought in from far away along its direction (turning or screwing in, when it does), without a collision with what is already placed (a press fit only as a fit: no thicker than one along a motion, and pushed in only where it overlaps in place). The parts are swept as rigid bodies; a pair a motion declares as flex may overlap while it moves, no deeper than declared, somewhere along it and never at an end of the range: how deep is measured, not whether the feature can bend that far", "G5": "each part alone, in the orientation it is exported in: no overhang steeper than 45° outside its declared overhangs_allowed boxes (which cover at most half of its surface), the part of every overhang steeper than 60° (where the A1's slicer adds supports by default